\section{Related Work}
\label{sec:related-work}

\paragraph{Self-Consistency and extensions.}
SC selects the most frequent answer across chain-of-thought traces \citep{wang2023sc}. Extensions include universal SC for free-form generation \citep{chen2024usc}, confidence weighting \citep{taubenfeld2025cisc}, diverse prompting with step-aware verification \citep{li2023diverse}, program-based vote filtering \citep{toh2024notallvotes}, and reasoning-aware filtering \citep{wan2024rasc, kim2026reasc}. \citet{loo2025reevaluating} show that SC gains plateau early. Our Condorcet analysis explains this: $\kappa = 0.21$--$0.82$ compresses $K_{\text{eff}}$ to 1.20--3.62 for $K = 12$ (\S\ref{sec:effective-k}).

\paragraph{Neuro-symbolic reasoning.}
Logic-LM \citep{pan2023logiclm} and LINC \citep{olausson2023linc} translate problems into formal logic for external provers; LINC documents ${\sim}$40\% translation errors. Recent extensions---CLOVER \citep{ryu2025clover}, DyLoS \citep{xu2026dylos}, Aristotle \citep{li2025aristotle}, FoVer \citep{wang2025fover}, VERGE \citep{singh2026verge}, LogicAgent \citep{luo2025logicagent}---add compositional translation, solver selection, decomposition, trained verifiers, and formal refinement, each introducing capabilities beyond the reasoning model. \citet{amonkar2025realitycheck} show that LLM formalization degrades with complexity; \citet{chan2026position} argue that logical soundness is not a reliable criterion for neurosymbolic verification with LLMs. Our oracle controls confirm the mechanism is sound ($+29.90$/$+14.22$\,pp FOLIO, $+11.50$\,pp ProofWriter); the failure localizes to self-extraction quality (\S\ref{sec:oracle}).

\paragraph{Test-time compute and verification.}
Scaling test-time computation through additional traces \citep{snell2025scaling} faces the same correlation challenge: same-model attempts collapse into correlated solutions. Reasoning models (o1, DeepSeek-R1 \citep{guo2025deepseekr1}, QwQ \citep{qwen2024qwq}) extend thinking time but remain subject to the independence bottleneck: QwQ-32B produces $\kappa = 0.91$ and $C_0 = 2.6\%$, suggesting that longer reasoning chains intensify homogenization rather than alleviating it. Trained verifiers offer an alternative \citep{cobbe2021gsm8k, lightman2024prm, wang2024mathshepherd}; multi-agent debate refines answers through discussion \citep{liang2023encouraging, du2023improving}. A natural hypothesis is that deterministic formal verification---where a Z3 solver provides logically guaranteed judgments---might bypass natural-language self-correction limitations by introducing a non-neural reasoning channel. We test this systematically and find the bottleneck shifts from the verifier to the extractor: self-extracted constraints inherit the model's bias regardless of verification formalism (\S\ref{sec:confirmation-bias}). More broadly, self-correction without external feedback degrades performance \citep{huang2024selfcorrect, stechly2025selfverification}; our quantitative diagnostics (BR, Eff-$K$, process-$\kappa$) provide reusable tools for predicting when any trace-aggregation method will fail.

\paragraph{CJT and ensemble diversity.}
CJT \citep{condorcet1785} guarantees convergence under independent voting; \citet{ladha1992correlated} prove correlated voters reduce effective ensemble size; \citet{lefort2024condorcet_llm} apply CJT to LLM classification. We extend this by quantifying \emph{why} self-correction fails---same-model traces are correlated voters ($K_{\text{eff}}$ collapses)---and showing this persists even under formal verification (Z3-checked symbolic constraints) and at the process level (\S\ref{sec:process-kappa}).

\paragraph{Positioning.}
Prior self-correction studies \citep{huang2024selfcorrect, stechly2025selfverification} establish qualitative negative results; we contribute reusable quantitative diagnostics that characterize the failure mode. Effective-$K$ (Eq.~\ref{eq:effk}) measures how much independent information $K$ traces actually carry. The bias ratio ($\text{BR}$; Eq.~\ref{eq:mirage}) quantifies the degree to which self-extracted constraints post-hoc rationalize the model's answer rather than independently verify it, connecting symbolic extraction to CoT faithfulness concerns \citep{turpin2024language}. Conclusion leakage rate ($C_D$) isolates answer-dependent constraint contamination at the step level. Together, these diagnostics show that formal Z3-checked verification inherits the same bias ($\text{BR} = 4.97\times$)---a finding invisible to prior work that examines only natural-language self-correction. The cross-architecture escape (\S\ref{sec:cross-arch}) yields a capability gap corollary: external verification helps only when the verifier's standalone accuracy exceeds the generator's SC baseline, providing a practical decision criterion absent from existing frameworks.

